.TH DISCO 1 "November 2026" "D!sco 0.11.1" "D!sco (Distro Custom)"
.SH NAME
disco \- D!sco (Distro Custom): build your own Debian or Devuan distribution
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B disco
[\fB\-p\fR \fIPROJECT\fR] [\fB\-D\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
.br
.B disco-pkexec
[\fIPROJECT\fR|\fIISO\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
D!sco builds your own distribution from Debian (stable, testing, sid) or Devuan
with Debian's own tools (mmdebstrap or debootstrap, chroot, mksquashfs, xorriso,
live-build): a hybrid live ISO for PCs and UEFI machines (amd64, i386, arm64,
riscv64) or an SD-card image for the Raspberry Pi. Other processors are built
through qemu-user (binfmt_misc). A project holds the system (\fIrootfs/\fR), the
ISO tree (\fIiso/\fR), package lists (\fIlists/\fR), files copied into the system
(\fIoverlay/\fR), scripts (\fIhooks/\fR), own packages (\fIdebs/\fR), boot images,
caches, logs and the built images (\fIoutput/\fR). Ubuntu and Ubuntu-based images
are refused. The old commands \fBdistroforge\fR and \fBeduka-customizer\fR start D!sco.
.PP
Without a command the graphical interface starts. Most commands need
administrator rights.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B gui [PROJECT|ISO]
Start the graphical interface.
.TP
.B new [PATH] [\-\-preset NAME] [\-\-platform ID] [\-\-iso FILE | \-\-bootstrap SUITE [\-\-devuan] | \-\-snapshot dist|backup]
Create a project from a preset, a Debian or Debian-based live ISO, a new Debian or
Devuan base (mmdebstrap) or a copy of the running system.
.TP
.B platforms
List what D!sco builds for: pc64, pc32, arm64-efi, rpi-arm64, rpi5, rpi-armhf,
rpi-armel, riscv64-efi.
.TP
.B presets [list|show|apply|save|delete|export] [NAME] [\-\-file FILE]
Presets for automated builds: the choices of a distribution and its package lists, saved under a name.
.TP
.B builder [\-\-name N] [\-\-platform ID] [\-\-family debian|devuan] [\-\-suite S] [\-\-desktop ID|none] [\-\-init I] [\-\-installer calamares|none|debs] [\-\-method disco|live-build] [\-\-mirror URL]
Show or change the choices used by build-all (automated builds from the command line).
.TP
.B lists [show|new|add|remove|on|off|delete|install|catalog] [LIST] [PACKAGE...]
The package lists of the distribution (\fIlists/NN-name.list\fR): one package per
line, \fB#\fR comments, \fB\-name\fR removes a package.
.TP
.B step prepare|base|packages|overlay|image
Run one step of the build.
.TP
.B build-all [\-\-rebuild-base]
Every step: prepare, base (when there is none), packages, overlay and scripts,
then the ISO or SD-card image.
.TP
.B live-build export|build
Write the live-build configuration (\fIlive-build/\fR), or build the ISO with
Debian's live-build.
.TP
.B info
Show the project, the detected system and the last ISO.
.TP
.B shell [COMMAND...]
Open an interactive root shell inside the image.
.TP
.B run COMMAND...
Run one command inside the image.
.TP
.B hook [SCRIPT...]
Run hook scripts inside the image (default: \fIPROJECT/hooks/*\fR).
.TP
.B sources \-\-suite stable|testing|sid [\-\-backports] [\-\-deb\-src] [\-\-mirror URL]
Write a clean deb822 \fI/etc/apt/sources.list.d/debian.sources\fR.
\fB\-\-add\fR \fINAME\fR \fB\-\-uri\fR \fIURI\fR \fB\-\-suites\fR \fIS\fR [\fB\-\-key\fR \fIURL|FILE\fR]
adds a third-party repository.
.TP
.B apt install|remove|upgrade|update|deb|list|search|file ...
Manage Debian packages inside the image.
.TP
.B flatpak setup|install|remove|list|search [APP-ID...] [\-\-firstboot]
Flathub applications, installed into the image or on first boot.
.TP
.B desktop catalog|install|session|dm|list|session-type|compositor|sddm-theme [NAME] [\-\-edition mini|compact|full|full_apps] [\-\-type x11|wayland] [\-\-preset P]
Desktop environments, window managers, sessions, login screens, X11/Wayland and compositors.
\fBinstall\fR takes an edition: Mini, Compact, Full (default) or Full with apps.
.TP
.B apps roles|status|replace ROLE PACKAGE [\-\-remove PKG...] [\-\-remove\-old]
Replace a default application (browser, mail, office, spreadsheet, editor, files,
terminal, images, video, music, pdf, archive, calculator): install it, make it the
default for its file types and Debian alternatives, and remove the old ones.
.TP
.B eduka-desktop [\-\-repo URL|DIR] [\-\-ref REF] [\-\-deb FILE] [\-\-set SECTION.KEY=VALUE]
Fetch, build and install Eduka-Desktop and set its defaults for new users.
.TP
.B brand identity|plymouth|plymouth-generate|wallpaper|login|locale VALUES...
Identity (os-release), Plymouth themes, wallpaper, login screen and locale.
.TP
.B branding apply|generate|build|key|show [\-\-logo F] [\-\-wallpaper F] [\-\-keyring \-\-email E]
Build and install the <id>-branding package (identity of base-files, lsb-release,
distro-info-data, desktop-base, Debian logos, GRUB, Calamares) and optionally
<id>-archive-keyring. The editable source lives in PROJECT/branding/.
.TP
.B workshop open|build|restore|list [PACKAGE] [\-\-no\-hold]
Copy an installed package to PROJECT/workshop/PACKAGE for direct editing,
rebuild and install it (held by default), or restore Debian's version.
.TP
.B themes list|apply|packs|import [ITEMS...] [\-\-gtk T] [\-\-icons T] [\-\-cursor T] [\-\-font F] [\-\-dark]
Default look for all desktops, theme packs and theme import.
.TP
.B language list|show|set [LOCALE] [\-\-extra L...] [\-\-timezone TZ] [\-\-keyboard K] [\-\-variant V] [\-\-no\-packs] [\-\-boot\-menu L...|all] [\-\-no\-calamares]
Default language, keyboard, time zone, translations, the Language submenu of
the ISO boot menu and the Calamares defaults.
.TP
.B purpose list|show ID|apply ID [\-\-only KEY,KEY] [\-\-edition minimal|full|full_apps]
What the distribution is for (education, server, professional, home, other) and its
recommendations (desktop, session, compositor, look, apps, flatpak, firmware, installer, plymouth).
.TP
.B assets FILES...
Add themes, icon and cursor themes, fonts, wallpapers, Plymouth and SDDM themes
from files, folders or archives; each is placed where it belongs.
.TP
.B wallpapers list|add FILES|default NAME|remove NAME
The wallpaper gallery of the image and its default.
.TP
.B users show|live NAME|live\-remove|add NAME|passwd NAME|delete NAME [\-\-fullname F] [\-\-no\-password] [\-\-password\-stdin] [\-\-debian\-default] [\-\-no\-autologin] [\-\-groups G,G] [\-\-admin] [\-\-shell S] [\-\-keep\-home]
The live user (with a password, without a password or Debian's default) and
accounts in the image. Passwords are asked for, or read from standard input
with \-\-password\-stdin; \-\-no\-password creates a user without a password.
.TP
.B calamares show|install|set MODULE KEY=VALUE...|branding|slides FILES|users|partition|live\-password [PASSWORD]
Edit the Calamares installer. Values are YAML, e.g.
.B calamares users min_length=8 autologin=false
or
.B calamares set welcome requirements="{requiredStorage: 15}".
.TP
.B plymouth list|install SOURCE...|apply NAME|remove NAME|packages [PKG...]|preview NAME [\-\-apply] [\-\-seconds N]
Plymouth themes from .deb, .zip, .tar.*, folders or Debian packages.
.TP
.B kernel list|available|install PKG...|third\-party backports|liquorix|xanmod|xanmod\-lts|deb FILES|remove VERSION|iso VERSION|initramfs|firmware|grub KEY=VALUE... [\-\-headers]
Kernels of the image and the GRUB defaults of the installed system.
.TP
.B bootmenu list|show FILE|edit FILE [\-\-from F] [\-\-once]|revert FILE|apply
Edit GRUB, ISOLINUX and EFI image boot files (e.g. efi.img:EFI/boot/grub.cfg);
.B apply
rebuilds the ISO in seconds without recompressing the system.
.TP
.B live [\-\-session S] [\-\-resolution WxH] [\-\-mode skel|root|sandbox]
Run the image's desktop in a nested Xephyr window; changes are saved into the image.
.TP
.B sounds events|themes|show|set|add|clear|apply|remove [ITEMS] [\-\-theme T] [\-\-no\-boot] [\-\-no\-login] [\-\-no\-shutdown]
System sounds (boot, login, logout, shutdown, errors, notifications, devices) as the default sound theme.
.TP
.B welcome show|export|import|apply|remove [FILE]
Welcome screen with four pages shown after login (design as JSON).
.TP
.B grub-theme list|check|add|use|remove [THEME] [\-\-installed]
Third-party GRUB themes; incompatible themes are refused with the reasons.
.TP
.B init list|use [systemd|sysvinit|openrc|runit]
The init system of the image, with everything that has to change with it.
.TP
.B boot-loader list|show|set|install|remove|use [ID] [KEY=VALUE...]
Boot loaders of installed systems: grub, grub-secureboot, systemd-boot, refind, efistub,
syslinux. \fBuse\fR installs it into the image and makes the Calamares installer put it on
computers; \fBset\fR changes its settings (for example TIMEOUT=3 CMDLINE="quiet splash").
.TP
.B calamares check
A careful check of the Calamares installer against the image.
.TP
.B check [\-\-deep] [\-\-fix]
Check the image before building: what would make the build fail, the ISO not
boot or private data leak into it. With \-\-fix, fix automatically what can be
fixed and check again. Exits with 1 when there are problems.
.TP
.B build [\-\-target\-size smallest|none|MB] [\-\-compression zstd|xz|gzip|lz4|lzo] [\-\-boot\-mode auto|replay|generate] [\-\-skip\-checks] ...
Check, then build the hybrid BIOS/UEFI ISO image (for Raspberry Pi platforms:
the SD-card image, compressed with xz, with its SHA-256 checksum). \-\-target\-size (for example
100, 300, 500, 700, 1000, 4400) chooses the fastest lossless compression that
should reach that size in megabytes.
.TP
.B test [\-\-firmware uefi|bios|secureboot] [\-\-disk]
Boot the image in QEMU.
.TP
.B recipe apply|export [FILE]
Apply or export a JSON recipe (reproducible builds).
.TP
.B clean [\-\-unmount\-only] [\-\-all] [\-\-keep\-iso [\-y]]
Unmount everything and remove caches (or the whole tree). \-\-keep\-iso deletes everything of a
finished project but its ISO images and their checksums.
.TP
.B doctor [\-\-fix]
Check (and install) the host tools.
.TP
.B download [\-\-suite stable|testing] [\-\-list] [FILE]
Download and verify an official Debian live image.
.TP
.B about
Version, license, credits and how to support the project.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/disco/disco.conf
Global settings (Debian codenames, mirrors, Eduka-Desktop repository, build defaults).
.TP
.I /usr/share/disco/exclude.list
Paths excluded from the squashfs.
.TP
.I PROJECT/project.json
Project state and history.
.TP
.I /tmp/disco/
Developer logs: disco.log, errors.log and bug reports.
.TP
.I /usr/share/disco/guide/Disco-Guide.pdf
User guide with pictures.
.TP
.I /etc/distroforge-bootloader.conf, /usr/sbin/distroforge-bootloader
In the image: the boot loader the installer sets up, and the program that does it.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
sudo disco new /home/disco/mypi \-\-preset "Raspberry Pi desktop (Pi 3, 4, 400)"
sudo disco -p /home/disco/mypi lists add applications thonny
sudo disco -p /home/disco/mypi build-all
sudo disco new ~/mylinux \-\-iso debian-live-13.1.0-amd64-standard.iso
sudo disco -p ~/mylinux desktop install xfce \-\-edition full_apps
sudo disco -p ~/mylinux apps replace browser chromium \-\-remove-old
sudo disco -p ~/mylinux flatpak install org.kde.gcompris \-\-firstboot
sudo disco -p ~/mylinux check \-\-fix
sudo disco -p ~/mylinux build \-\-target\-size 700
disco -p ~/mylinux test \-\-firmware uefi
.fi
.SH NOTES
The graphical interface collects changes in step 14, Review & Apply, and applies
them together; the commands apply each change at once. D!sco was called
Eduka-Customizer until 0.17 Alpha; the commands \fBeduka-customizer\fR and
\fBeduka-customizer-pkexec\fR still work.
